# Style Forage: Design System & Style Guide

A guide to the visual language and user experience principles of Style Forage.

## Tailwind v4 Configuration

Custom theme values are defined in `index.css` using `@theme` blocks. When adding new design tokens:

```css
@theme {
  --color-custom-name: #hexvalue;
  --font-custom: 'Font Name', fallback;
}
```

## Color Palette

The palette is inspired by natural textures (Sage, Sand, Stone) to evoke a sense of calm, high-end sophistication.

| Name | Variable | Hex | Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Sage 500** | `bg-sage-500` | `#8cae8c` | Primary actions, accents, active states. |
| **Sage 50** | `bg-sage-50` | `#f4f7f4` | Soft backgrounds, UI containers. |
| **Stone 900** | `text-stone-900` | `#1c1917` | Primary headings, dark backgrounds. |
| **Stone 500** | `text-stone-500` | `#78716c` | Body text, secondary information. |
| **Sand 100** | `bg-sand-100` | `#f7f1e6` | Tertiary backgrounds, warm accents. |

## Typography

We use a "Serif for Soul, Sans for Clarity" approach.

- **Serif: Playfair Display**
  - *Usage*: Main headings, quotes, brand logo.
  - *Feel*: Elegant, editorial, timeless.
- **Sans: Inter**
  - *Usage*: Body text, buttons, form labels, metadata.
  - *Feel*: Modern, highly legible, professional.

## Layout & Components

### 1. Spacing
- Sections use consistent vertical padding (`py-24` or `py-32`).
- Grids typically use a `gap-8` (32px) for a breathable, "foraged" feel.

### 2. Cards & Containers
- **Border Radius**: Large radii are preferred (`rounded-3xl` for cards, `rounded-full` for buttons).
- **Shadows**: Subtle `shadow-sm` by default, upgrading to `shadow-xl` or `shadow-2xl` on hover to imply depth.
- **Borders**: Soft borders using `border-stone-100` to define space without harsh lines.

### 3. Buttons

**IMPORTANT: Always use the `Button` component from `@/components/ui/Button.tsx` for all buttons.** Do not create custom `<button>` elements with inline styles. This ensures consistent styling, accessibility, and maintainability.

```tsx
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
```

**Available Variants:**

| Variant | Usage | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `primary` | CTAs, main actions | Dark background, white text. High contrast. |
| `secondary` | Secondary actions | Sage background for less prominent actions. |
| `outline` | Tertiary actions | Bordered, transparent background. |
| `ghost` | Cancel buttons, subtle actions | Text only with subtle hover effect. |
| `light` | On dark backgrounds | White background, dark text. |
| `icon` | Edit, preview, settings | Icon-only button with sage hover. |
| `icon-danger` | Delete actions | Icon-only button with red hover. |
| `chip` | Unselected filter/category | Stone background for selection chips. |
| `chip-selected` | Selected filter/category | Sage background for selected chips. |

**Available Sizes:**

| Size | Usage |
| :--- | :--- |
| `sm` | Compact UI areas |
| `md` | Default for most buttons |
| `lg` | Prominent CTAs |
| `icon` | Icon-only buttons (square, use with `icon` or `icon-danger` variant) |

**Examples:**

```tsx
// Primary action button
<Button variant="primary" size="md">Save Changes</Button>

// Cancel button (ghost style)
<Button variant="ghost" size="md">Cancel</Button>

// Icon button for editing
<Button variant="icon" size="icon" title="Edit">
  <Edit3 size={16} />
</Button>

// Icon button for deleting
<Button variant="icon-danger" size="icon" title="Delete">
  <Trash2 size={16} />
</Button>

// Full-width submit button
<Button variant="primary" size="lg" fullWidth>Submit</Button>

// Selection chip (category, season, filter)
<Button
  variant={isSelected ? 'chip-selected' : 'chip'}
  size="sm"
  onClick={() => setSelected(!isSelected)}
>
  Category Name
</Button>
```

**Rules:**
1. **Never use raw `<button>` elements** - always use the `Button` component.
2. **Always include `title` or `aria-label`** for icon-only buttons.
3. **Use appropriate variants** - `ghost` for cancel, `icon-danger` for delete.
4. **Cursor handling is automatic** - the component includes `cursor-pointer` and `disabled:cursor-not-allowed`.

### 4. Action sheet (bottom sheet) modal

Use a single pattern for slide-up modals that reveal lists or detail content (e.g. Shopping List, Shop Links, Tips, Read more caption). Keeps mobile UX consistent and recognizable. Implement via the shared `ActionSheet` component in `Lookbook.tsx` so behavior is consistent.

**Behavior:**

- **Open:** Panel animates up with `animate-slide-up` (0.3s ease-out). Backdrop is `bg-black/50`.
- **Close:** When the user taps backdrop, close button, or swipes down to close, the panel runs `animate-slide-down` (0.3s ease-in), the backdrop fades out (`opacity-0` + `transition-opacity duration-300`), then `onClose` is called after 300ms so the parent can unmount.
- **Swipe to close (mobile):** If the user swipes down on the panel and the body content is scrolled to the top (scrollTop ≤ 2), and the swipe distance exceeds the threshold (~80px), the sheet closes with the same close animation. This avoids closing when the user is scrolling the list.

**Structure:**

1. **Backdrop:** `fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black/50 transition-opacity duration-300`; when exiting add `opacity-0 pointer-events-none`. `onClick` to start close.
2. **Panel:** `absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 bg-white rounded-t-3xl max-h-[85vh] overflow-hidden flex flex-col`; use `animate-slide-up` when opening and `animate-slide-down` when exiting. `onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}`. Attach `onTouchStart` and `onTouchEnd` for swipe-to-close (record touch Y and body scrollTop at start; at end, if deltaY > threshold and was at top, start close).
3. **Header (flex-shrink-0):**
   - Drag handle: `w-12 h-1 bg-stone-300 rounded-full mx-auto mb-4`
   - Row: `flex items-center justify-between` with title and close button.
   - Title: `font-serif text-lg text-stone-900` (e.g. "Shopping List", "Caption").
   - Close button: `p-2 -mr-2 text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 cursor-pointer`, `<X size={24} />`, `aria-label="Close"`.
   - Wrapper: `p-4 border-b border-stone-100 flex-shrink-0`.
4. **Body:** `flex-1 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden p-4 min-h-0` (ref for scrollTop check). Optional `bodyClassName` for scrollbar styling (e.g. `caption-modal-body`).

**Example (Caption):**
```tsx
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
import { X } from 'lucide-react';

{isOpen && (
  <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black/50" onClick={onClose}>
    <div
      className="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 bg-white rounded-t-3xl max-h-[85vh] overflow-hidden animate-slide-up flex flex-col"
      onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
    >
      <div className="p-4 border-b border-stone-100 flex-shrink-0">
        <div className="w-12 h-1 bg-stone-300 rounded-full mx-auto mb-4" />
        <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 className="font-serif text-lg text-stone-900">Title</h3>
          <Button variant="ghost" size="icon" onClick={onClose} aria-label="Close" className="-mr-2">
            <X size={24} />
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4">{/* content */}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

**Usage:** Shopping List, Shop Links, Tips, and “Read more” caption in the Lookbook viewer all use this pattern. When adding new slide-up content (e.g. filters, details), reuse this structure.

### 5. Selection Chips
Pill-shaped interactive elements for selecting dates, times, or options. Uses an **outline style** for selected state to maintain visual clarity without heavy fills.

**Structure:**
- Shape: `rounded-full` (pill)
- Border: `border-2` always present (transparent when unselected, visible when selected)
- Padding: `py-3 px-4` for standard chips, custom sizing for date chips

**States:**

| State | Classes | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Default** | `border-transparent bg-stone-50 text-stone-700` | Unselected, available option |
| **Hover** | `hover:bg-stone-100` | Interactive feedback |
| **Selected** | `border-stone-900 bg-white text-stone-900` | Outline style - dark border, white background |
| **Disabled** | `border-transparent bg-stone-50 text-stone-300 line-through cursor-not-allowed` | Unavailable option with strikethrough |

**Example (Time Slot):**
```tsx
<button className={`
  py-3 px-4 rounded-full border-2 transition-all
  ${isSelected 
    ? 'border-stone-900 bg-white text-stone-900' 
    : isDisabled
      ? 'border-transparent bg-stone-50 text-stone-300 line-through cursor-not-allowed'
      : 'border-transparent bg-stone-50 text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-100'
  }
`}>
  {label}
</button>
```

**Usage Guidelines:**
- Use for date pickers, time slots, multi-select options, and filter chips
- Outline style keeps UI clean and allows multiple selections to be visible without overwhelming
- Always include `transition-all` for smooth state changes
- Always include `cursor-pointer` for selectable/clickable chips (and `cursor-not-allowed` for disabled).
- Include proper `aria-pressed` and `aria-label` for accessibility
- Show selection count when multi-select is enabled

## Cursor & interactivity

All button-like and clickable elements must show the pointer cursor on hover so users know they are interactive.

| Element | Cursor | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Buttons (primary, secondary, outline, chips) | `cursor-pointer` | Required on `<button>`, `role="button"`, and any clickable element. |
| Disabled buttons / unavailable options | `cursor-not-allowed` | Pair with `disabled:pointer-events-none` when appropriate. |
| Links | `cursor-pointer` | Default for `<a>`; ensure custom link-styled elements include it. |

**Rule:** When adding or updating any interactive control (buttons, selection chips, nav items, icon buttons, submit inputs), include `cursor-pointer` in the className. For disabled state, include `cursor-not-allowed`.

## Visual Signatures

- **Glassmorphism**: The header uses `backdrop-blur-md` with `bg-white/95` to feel integrated with the content below it.
- **Micro-animations**: Subtle `hover:-translate-y-2` on cards and `animate-fade-in` on page loads to provide a premium, reactive feel.
- **Imagery**: High-quality, editorial fashion photography with generous whitespace.

## Admin Card Design Best Practices

### 1. Card Structure & Layout
Admin cards should follow a consistent structure with content on the left and actions on the right.

**Layout Pattern:**
```tsx
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
import { Edit3, Trash2 } from 'lucide-react';

<div className="p-4 md:p-6">
  <div className="flex items-start justify-between mb-4">
    {/* Content Section */}
    <div className="flex-1 pr-4">
      <h3 className="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl text-stone-900 mb-2">
        {title}
      </h3>
      <p className="text-stone-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        {description}
      </p>
    </div>
    
    {/* Actions Section */}
    <div className="flex gap-2 flex-shrink-0">
      <Button variant="icon" size="icon" title="Edit">
        <Edit3 size={16} />
      </Button>
      <Button variant="icon-danger" size="icon" title="Delete">
        <Trash2 size={16} />
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  {/* Additional Content */}
  {children}
</div>
```

### 2. Action Button Guidelines

**Always use the `Button` component for action buttons:**

**Edit Button:**
- Variant: `icon`
- Size: `icon`
- Icon: `Edit3` size 16
- Purpose: Modify existing content
- Position: Right side, first button

**Delete Button:**
- Variant: `icon-danger`
- Size: `icon`
- Icon: `Trash2` size 16  
- Purpose: Remove content permanently
- Position: Right side, second button

**Button Examples:**
```tsx
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
import { Edit3, Trash2 } from 'lucide-react';

// Edit button
<Button variant="icon" size="icon" title="Edit" onClick={handleEdit}>
  <Edit3 size={16} />
</Button>

// Delete button  
<Button variant="icon-danger" size="icon" title="Delete" onClick={handleDelete}>
  <Trash2 size={16} />
</Button>
```

### 3. Content Organization

**Primary Content (Left):**
- Use `flex-1 pr-4` to take available space with right padding
- Title: `font-serif text-lg md:text-xl text-stone-900 mb-2`
- Description: `text-stone-600 text-sm leading-relaxed`
- Maintain visual hierarchy with proper spacing

**Actions (Right):**
- Use `flex gap-2 flex-shrink-0` for consistent spacing
- Buttons are `flex-shrink-0` to prevent compression
- Vertical alignment: `items-start` to align with content top

### 4. Card Container

**Base Card:**
```tsx
<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-stone-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
  {/* Card content */}
</div>
```

**Hover Effects:**
- Container: `hover:border-sage-200 hover:shadow-md transition-all`
- Actions: Individual hover states as defined above

### 5. Responsive Design

**Mobile (<md):**
- Padding: `p-4`
- Title: `text-lg`
- Actions: Standard size (16px icons)

**Desktop (≥md):**
- Padding: `p-6` 
- Title: `text-xl`
- Actions: Standard size (16px icons)

### 6. Examples

**LinkCard Admin View:**
```tsx
import { Button } from '../components/ui/Button';
import { Edit3, Trash2 } from 'lucide-react';

<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-stone-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
  <div className="p-4 md:p-6">
    <div className="flex items-start justify-between mb-4">
      <div className="flex-1 pr-4">
        <h3 className="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl text-stone-900 mb-2">
          {linkCard.title}
        </h3>
        <p className="text-stone-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          {linkCard.description}
        </p>
      </div>
      <div className="flex gap-2 flex-shrink-0">
        <Button
          variant="icon"
          size="icon"
          onClick={() => startEditingLinkCard(linkCard)}
          title="Edit"
        >
          <Edit3 size={16} />
        </Button>
        <Button
          variant="icon-danger"
          size="icon"
          onClick={() => handleDeleteLinkCard(linkCard.id)}
          title="Delete"
        >
          <Trash2 size={16} />
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    {/* Links content */}
    {linkCard.links.length > 0 && (
      <div className="space-y-3">
        {/* Link items */}
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
</div>
```

### 7. Accessibility Considerations

- **ARIA Labels:** Always include `title` attribute on action buttons
- **Keyboard Navigation:** Ensure buttons are focusable and have visible focus states
- **Color Contrast:** Maintain WCAG AA compliance with specified colors
- **Touch Targets:** Minimum 44px touch targets (current 32px with padding meets this)

### 8. Consistency Rules

1. **Always place actions on the right side** of the card content
2. **Use consistent spacing**: `gap-2` between action buttons
3. **Maintain visual hierarchy**: Content left, actions right
4. **Use consistent colors**: Sage for edit, red for delete
5. **Add proper hover states** for all interactive elements
6. **Include semantic titles** for screen readers

## Tone of Voice

- **Encouraging**: We don't judge closets; we curate confidence.
- **Actionable**: Every tip or service description should lead to a clear "next step."
- **Concise**: Respect the user's time. Clear, punchy headlines over long paragraphs.
